    "webkit-diagonal-axis-lock-input": {
      "status": "KNOWN_LIMITATION",
      "note": "Playwright WebKit delivers one pointermove of a diagonal axis-locked path from the 2nd drag; a capturing document listener sees one event too and the pre-fix code is identical, so events are lost before page code. WebKit uses a horizontal path for that scenario. On Linux CI WebKit the same input loss also hits four more scenarios (Y-only, snap points, press-during-release, pointercancel), which are skipped there only (CI=1) and still run on Chromium, Firefox and macOS WebKit. Not verified on a real Safari."
    },
